  "note": "Checkpoint two: family, divisions, mark and the printed label are fixed together here, before the figure shape is drawn. The label is the card's schematic line: '<Family> at <unit> <mark> of <divisions>'. The basis is a verbatim substring of that card's own record, naming the phrase that fixes the position; it never comes from another card.",
  "families": {
    "pipeline": "ordered stages joined in sequence; the marked stage is the one filled",
    "gate": "a decision with routes fanning out; the marked route is the one drawn solid",
    "matrix": "a grid of candidate cells; the marked cell is the one occupied",
    "gauge": "a dial of levels against a cap; the marked level is the arc filled",
    "rhythm": "a clock of repeated intervals; the marked beat is the heavy sector",
    "loop": "a cycle of nodes that returns to its start; the marked node is the heavy one",
    "ladder": "ranked rungs with a cutoff; the marked rung is the last one held",
    "threshold": "a curve that steps at a point; the marked point is where it changes"
  },
